# Graphify & Token Economy Protocol

To maximize intelligence throughput and minimize token consumption:

## 1. 90% Retrieval Rule
- Always inspect dependency graphs and symbol indexes (`graphify-out/`) before reading full source files.
- Never cat or read entire directories blindly.
- Use narrow AST queries to locate specific function signatures and interfaces.

## 2. Terse Communication (Caveman Mode)
- Provide direct, dense, actionable responses.
- Minimize conversational filler and boilerplate.
- Focus on concrete file paths, diffs, and verification commands.

## 3. Graph Maintenance
- When adding new modules or refactoring component boundaries, run `bash scripts/graphify_narrow.sh` to update index artifacts.
- Keep graph metadata lightweight and committed to version control where appropriate.
